   "type": "NAT",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Light is incident on a silicon sample starting at t = 0 s and generating excess carriers uniformly throughout the silicon for <sup>t</sup> > 0. The generation rate is g′ = 5 × 10<sup>21</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup> s<sup>–1</sup> at <sup>T</sup> = 300 K. The silicon is n-type with <em>N<sub>D</sub></em> = 5 × 10<sup>16</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>. If ni = 1.5 × 10<sup>10</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>, τ<em><sub>no</sub></em> = 10<sup>–6</sup> sec, τ<em><sub>po</sub></em> = 10<sup>–7</sup> sec, μ<em><sub>n</sub></em> = 1000 cm<sup>2</sup>/V-s and μ<sub><em>p</em> </sub>= 420 cm<sup>–2</sup>/V-s, then the value of conductivity at <em>t</em> = τ<em><sub>po</sub></em> is equal to ______<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3cd63926154e22a18d08.png\" /> (correct to one decimal place)</p>",
